# KazeSetu Backend Rules

## Architecture

- Backend follows a Modular Monolith architecture.
- Every feature is implemented as a module.
- Do not create additional Express applications.

## Module Structure

Each module must contain:

- controller
- service
- repository
- routes
- dto
- validator
- types

## Controllers

- No business logic.
- Validate request.
- Call service.
- Return response.

## Services

- All business logic belongs here.
- Services never communicate directly with Express.

## Repositories

- Only repositories access Prisma.
- No Prisma queries outside repositories.

## Validation

- Use Zod.
- Validate every request body, params, and query.

## Errors

- Throw typed application errors.
- Use centralized error middleware.

## Database

- PostgreSQL + Prisma.
- Use transactions where appropriate.
- Never expose Prisma models directly to clients.

## Code Style

- TypeScript strict mode.
- No `any`.
- Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Keep functions focused and small.